From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shuai Zhang <shuai.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:35:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] Bluetooth: hci_qca: Reopen the UART after enabling
 QCA2066

QCA2066 does not reopen the UART after the controller is enabled, which
causes RX/TX out-of-sync errors. The UART has to be reopened once the
controller is powered on.

qca_regulator_init() already enables the controller and then reopens the
UART, but QCA2066 does not go through it. QCA2066 was added with its own
SoC type and handled in the default case.

Let QCA2066 go through qca_regulator_init() as well, and handle it in the
other places that check the SoC type in the same way. This also applies
the baudrate switching, flow control, shutdown and probe handling of
those chips to QCA2066. btqca.c checks the SoC type in the same way, so
the firmware version is also shown in the log.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261110092929.234617-2-shuai.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com/
[shuai: struct qca_power is already flattened on this branch, so there is
 no bt_power allocation to extend, and the power off function is
 qca_power_shutdown()]
Signed-off-by: Shuai Zhang <shuai.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com>

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261110092929.234617-2-shuai.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com/]
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c   |  1 +
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
index 7affced..540181f 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
@@ -1067,6 +1067,7 @@ int qca_uart_setup(struct hci_dev *hdev, uint8_t baudrate,
 	switch (soc_type) {
 	case QCA_WCN3991:
 	case QCA_WCN6750:
+	case QCA_QCA2066:
 	case QCA_WCN6855:
 	case QCA_WCN7850:
 	case QCA_QCC2072:
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
index 5c8e569..f19a8cb 100644
